Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/51] B70-V6x: riceharvest patch_asym_gptq (inert unless a
 sym=false GPTQ checkpoint loads, B70_ASYM_GPTQ marker)

riceharvest/vllm b70/v0.32 43fb2ee310: load asymmetric GPTQ (sym=false,
uint4 + qzeros) on XPU through AutoGPTQ:
- TYPE_MAP gains (4, False) -> uint4 (before: "Unsupported quantization
  config" at load);
- the Marlin support check runs for symmetric configs only;
- the linear kernel config carries zero_points=not is_sym;
- on XPU, process_weights_after_loading adds the GPTQ v1 +1 back to every
  qzeros nibble (the kernel takes raw z).

B70-V6x change: the stock XPUwNa16 kernel transposes w_zp for every
zero-point layer; rice's commit dropped that transpose for all of them,
which would also change AWQ and compressed-tensors asym wNa16 on XPU. Here
the transpose is skipped only when AutoGPTQ flags the layer
(layer._b70_gptq_asym_zp, set only for sym=false on XPU), so every other
loader and every symmetric GPTQ checkpoint takes the stock path unchanged.
No env flag: with no asymmetric checkpoint loaded nothing changes.

Linear layers only; an asymmetric GPTQ MoE goes through AutoGPTQMoEMethod
with may_have_zp=True, which this commit does not touch. Not GPU-tested here.

Generated from patches/b70/patch_asym_gptq.py of
riceharvest/b70-qwen38-cookbook@9f7fa83.
